---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Experiments — DQN Flappy Bird Training Log
description: The numbered DQN experiment log — every change documented with hypothesis, configuration, results, and conclusion. Real training data from browser-trained agents.
section: experiments
keywords: ["experiment log", "ablation", "hyperparameters", "training results", "dqn experiments"]
---

<section class="container" data-reveal-root>
  <header class="page-head" data-reveal>
    <p class="kicker"><span class="kicker-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>Experiments · the public log</p>
    <h1>Experiments</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      One hypothesis per experiment. Each entry records what changed, why, what
      happened, and what was learned — preserved at a Git tag so the exact code that
      produced the result is always one click away.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section aria-labelledby="compare-heading" data-reveal>
    <h2 id="compare-heading" class="section-subhead">Comparison</h2>
    {% include "components/experiments-table.njk" %}
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="all-exp-heading" data-reveal>
    <h2 id="all-exp-heading" class="section-subhead">All experiments</h2>
    <div class="card-grid card-grid--2">
      {% for exp in experiments.list %}
      <div data-reveal>{% include "components/experiment-card.njk" %}</div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" aria-labelledby="how-exp-heading" data-reveal>
    <h2 id="how-exp-heading" class="section-subhead">How experiments are recorded</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Experiments live in the repository, not in the website. Adding a directory
        <code>experiments/004-slug/</code> with an <code>experiment.json</code>,
        a <code>README.md</code>, and a <code>runs/</code> folder is enough — this page
        and the detail page are generated automatically at the next build. The schema
        is documented in
        <a href="{{ site.repo }}/blob/main/experiments/README.md" rel="noopener">experiments/README.md</a>;
        larger training series live under
        <a href="{{ site.repo }}/tree/main/data" rel="noopener">data/</a>.
      </p>
      <pre><code>experiments/
└── 004-slug/
    ├── README.md          → objective · hypothesis · conclusion
    ├── experiment.json    → machine-readable configuration
    └── runs/
        └── 001.json       → run results, parameters, exploration</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>
</section>
